<code>assert this.size() > 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.comparator().compare(this.peek(), this.get(i)) <= 0;</code>

Explanation:
- The assertion checks if the queue is not empty (`this.size() > 0`).
- If the queue is not empty, it ensures that the element returned by `peek()` is less than or equal to every other element in the queue.
- This is achieved using a universal quantifier (`\forall`) to iterate over all indices `i` in the range `[0, this.size())` and comparing the `peek()` element with each element in the queue using the provided comparator (`this.comparator().compare(this.peek(), this.get(i)) <= 0`).
--------------------
<code>assert this.size() > 0 => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.comparator().compare(this.peek(), this.get(i)) <= 0;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.size() > 0 => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.comparator().compare(this.peek(), this.get(i)) <= 0;</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the queue is not empty, the element returned by `peek()` is less than or equal to every other element in the queue according to the comparator. If no comparator is provided, it defaults to the natural ordering of the elements.
